<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Randfontein Dec qtr pre-capex net rises.</title>
<headline>Randfontein Dec qtr pre-capex net rises.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Quarter to end-Dec versus preceding quarter</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Net profit before capital spending  43.83 vs 37.44</p>
<p>    Capital spending			  24.50 vs 24.63</p>
<p>Full name: Randfontein Estates Gold Mining Co Witwatersrand Ltd, managed by JCI Ltd</p>
<p>    Gold output (kg)			  5,100 vs 5,013</p>
<p>    Tonnes milled			 1,732,000 vs 1,770,000</p>
<p>    Yield (gram/t)			     2.94 vs 2.83</p>
<p>    Cost (rand/kg)			   49,620 vs 50,053</p>
<p>    Revenue (rand/kg)			56,068 vs 54,819</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said that the South Reef project was on schedule following the commencement of shaft sinking on Nov 18, while development of the 197 level station is well advanced.</p>
<p>The company also said that the roll out of the Business Process Re-engineering project to the other shafts had commenced following the completion of the pilot test site at Cooke 1 where results continued to be encouraging.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
